<section class="page container narrow legal">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Clear explanations about the personal information we use and the choices that are yours.</p>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: November 25, 2026</p>

  <p>EliteTap offers custom NFC and QR code business cards, along with hosted digital profiles. This policy describes how personal information is handled when you visit elitetap.ca, request a quote, place an order, use your client space or profile, or contact us.</p>
  <p class="callout"><strong>In short:</strong> we use your information to answer your requests, fulfil your orders and run your EliteTap profile. The site only uses essential cookies; no advertising or audience-measurement tool is turned on without your consent. We do not sell your information.</p>

  <h2>1. Responsible party and applicable laws</h2>
  <p>EliteTap, based in Laval (Quebec), is responsible for the personal information handled in its activities. Quebec's Act respecting the protection of personal information in the private sector, as amended by Law 25, governs these activities. The Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) may also apply to certain activities, such as interprovincial or international transactions.</p>
  <p>The role of person in charge of the protection of personal information belongs to the person with the highest authority in the business, unless delegated in writing. You can reach this person using the contact details in section 9.</p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Quote requests and communications:</strong> name, company, email, phone number if provided, card type and quantity, industry, message and files you choose to send, as well as exchanges by email or through the site chat.</li>
    <li><strong>Orders and customization:</strong> information needed to design the card or digital profile, files or logos provided, billing and shipping details, order details and service exchanges.</li>
    <li><strong>Client space and profile:</strong> login credentials and the information you choose to show on your public profile (name, title, contact details, photo, links). This information is visible to anyone who taps your card or opens your link.</li>
    <li><strong>Profile statistics:</strong> when a profile is opened, we record the date, the type of action (open, contact saved, link clicked) and an anonymous identifier that changes every day. We do not keep visitors' IP addresses.</li>
    <li><strong>Leads:</strong> when a visitor fills in a profile's "Leave your details" form and ticks the consent box, their name, contact details and message are sent to the profile owner. EliteTap keeps them on the owner's behalf for up to <?= (int) config('lead_retention_days', 730) ?> days. The consent text and date are recorded.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter:</strong> your email and proof of your consent (date and accepted text), only if you subscribe and confirm.</li>
    <li><strong>Browsing:</strong> technical data needed for the site to work securely.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment:</strong> information needed to track a transaction. Online payments are processed by Stripe; EliteTap never sees or stores your card number.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Please do not send us sensitive information that is not needed for your project.</p>

  <h2>3. Why we use this information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Answer questions and prepare quotes.</li>
    <li>Create and customize NFC cards, QR codes and digital profiles at your request.</li>
    <li>Manage orders, billing, delivery and after-sales service.</li>
    <li>Run your client space, profile, statistics and leads.</li>
    <li>Send you the newsletter, if you subscribed.</li>
    <li>Keep the site secure and working.</li>
    <li>Meet our accounting, tax and legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We ask for consent where the law requires it. Browsing the site does not, on its own, amount to consent to every use of your personal information. We do not sell your personal information.</p>

  <h2>4. Cookies and audience measurement</h2>
  <p>The site only uses strictly necessary cookies: one to keep you signed in to your client space and protect forms, and one to remember your language. Your choice on the cookie notice is stored in your browser.</p>
  <p>No advertising, third-party tracking or audience-measurement cookies are used at this time. If we add an audience-measurement tool (for example Google Analytics), it will only be turned on after your consent, which you can give, refuse or change at any time, and this policy will be updated.</p>

  <h2>5. Service providers and disclosures</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Web host:</strong> hosting of the site, profiles, database and forms.</li>
    <li><strong>Email services:</strong> sending and receiving email, including the newsletter.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe:</strong> online payment processing.</li>
    <li><strong>Carriers:</strong> order delivery.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Depending on the provider, information may be stored or processed outside Quebec, including in other provinces or countries where different rules may apply. We assess such transfers and take the measures required by law. We may also disclose information where the law allows or requires it.</p>

  <h2>6. Retention and destruction</h2>
  <p>We keep information only as long as needed for the purposes described or to meet our legal obligations. Your profile is kept while your account is active. Once the purposes are fulfilled and no retention obligation applies, information is destroyed or anonymized as required by law.</p>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>We apply reasonable measures suited to the sensitivity of the information, including secure connections (HTTPS), encrypted passwords, access limited to each employee's role and the use of service providers. No computer system can guarantee zero risk. In the event of a confidentiality incident, we take the appropriate steps, including the assessments, records and notices required by law.</p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Request access to the personal information we hold about you.</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate, incomplete or ambiguous information.</li>
    <li>Withdraw consent where processing relies on it (for example, unsubscribe from the newsletter with the link in every email).</li>
    <li>Request that dissemination stop, de-indexing or certain deletions where the legal conditions are met; you can also make your profile private from your client space.</li>
    <li>Where the law provides, request your computerized personal information in a structured, commonly used format (portability).</li>
    <li>File a complaint about how your personal information is handled.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We generally answer access or correction requests within 30 days. We may need to verify your identity. You may also consult the <a href="https://www.cai.gouv.qc.ca/" rel="noopener">Commission d'accès à l'information du Québec</a>.</p>

  <h2>9. Contact us</h2>
  <p><strong>Person in charge of the protection of personal information</strong><br>EliteTap management<br>Laval, Quebec, Canada<br>Email: <a href="mailto:info@elitetap.ca">info@elitetap.ca</a><br>Website: <a href="https://elitetap.ca/">elitetap.ca</a></p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>This policy may change with our practices, services or obligations. The updated version will be published here with its new revision date. Where a change requires specific notice or new consent, we will take the required steps.</p>
</section>
